hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17673","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, who said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, from Abu Isra'il, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque while Abu Isra'il was praying. It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Here he is, O Messenger of Allah; he does not sit, does not speak to people, does not seek shade, and he intends fasting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let him sit, speak to people, seek shade, and fast."
